From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Noronha Silva <gustavo@noronha.dev.br>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:15:23 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] egl/dri2: fail eglExportDMABUFImageMESA when the driver
 cannot export an fd

dri2_export_dma_buf_image_mesa ignored the return value of the
__DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD query and returned EGL_TRUE with the caller's fd array
untouched, so a driver that cannot export an image (virgl refuses one whose guest
storage is a stub) reported success and the caller went on to use an
uninitialized value as a file descriptor. GTK4 built a GdkDmabufTexture around
0xFFFF00FF, failed the download, and handed back a broken texture instead of
falling back.

Return EGL_FALSE, matching the adjacent stride and offset handling and the
extension's contract: close any fds already exported for earlier planes, set every
slot to -1, and release the plane image and display lock like the success path.
GTK now logs the failure and falls back to a GL readback, which is correct.

No EGL error is recorded, matching the existing early return when the image is not
exportable at all; whether both should raise EGL_BAD_ACCESS is a question for
upstream review.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
index 8185b79bfed..3fd0293f891 100644
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
@@ -2591,9 +2591,24 @@ dri2_export_dma_buf_image_mesa(_EGLDisplay *disp, _EGLImage *img, int *fds,
           *    "If the number of fds is less than the number of planes, then
           *    subsequent fd slots should contain -1."
           */
-         if (i == 0 || is_disjoint)
-            dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD, &fds[i]);
-         else
+         if (i == 0 || is_disjoint) {
+            if (!dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD, &fds[i])) {
+               /* The driver cannot export this image. Returning EGL_TRUE here
+                * would leave the caller's fd array untouched, and the caller
+                * would then use an uninitialized value as an fd.
+                */
+               if (i)
+                  dri2_destroy_image(image);
+               for (int j = 0; j < i; j++) {
+                  if (fds[j] >= 0)
+                     close(fds[j]);
+                  fds[j] = -1;
+               }
+               fds[i] = -1;
+               mtx_unlock(&dri2_dpy->lock);
+               return EGL_FALSE;
+            }
+         } else
             fds[i] = -1;
       }
 
